## 5. MCP and Roboflow

The course also introduces the concept of using **MCP** with development tools such as **Roboflow**.

**MCP (Model Context Protocol)** provides a standardized way for AI applications to connect with external tools, services, and data sources.

In an agentic development workflow, this can allow an AI assistant to interact with tools beyond simple text generation.

In the context of Computer Vision, integrations with platforms such as Roboflow can potentially support workflows involving:

- Computer Vision datasets
- Model development
- Image processing
- Model inference
- Dataset management
- Computer Vision pipelines
- Development automation

This section will be expanded as MCP and Roboflow are covered further during the SAM3 course.

